# Test strategy for {{ project_name }}

Status: incomplete installation seed. Select tests from the actual architecture,
requirements and risks before activating the quality profile. Do not substitute
a coverage percentage or a test name for behavioral evidence.

## Required project decisions

- Map acceptance criteria and critical risks to automated, manual or hybrid tests.
- Select unit/component tests for local logic and integration/contract tests for
  relevant module, database and external-service boundaries.
- Identify critical user/business flows needing end-to-end or acceptance tests.
- Include relevant success, rejection, boundary, permission, timeout and recovery
  scenarios. Bug repairs need an observed failing regression and repaired result.
- Select security, load, migration, restore and platform-matrix tests where their
  risks apply. Set justified measurable goals and document remaining coverage gaps.
- Record environments, isolated/redacted test data, prerequisites, test owners,
  actual workflow check IDs and reproducible evidence locations.
- Assign fast required PR checks, post-merge checks, scheduled larger suites and
  release/deployment checks according to the project's delivery contract.

## Agentic development

When the `agentic` profile applies, cover the real handoff chain: instruction and
profile context, dispatch, bounded worker execution, independent review, triage,
confirmed repair, Delta review, gate results and owner/orchestrator feedback.
Cover interruption, missing context/evidence, unauthorized actions and resume
behavior. State which paths use fixtures and which actually ran on the intended
host/provider; model output and mocked success are not runtime proof.

## Evidence and maintenance

Keep requirement/risk/rule-to-test links in `traceability.csv`. Commands and their
bounds remain in `.engineering-backbone/workflows.json`; reference their check IDs
here without maintaining a second command contract. Record actual revisions,
commands, exit codes, coverage and failures in approved CI/review artifacts.
An independent reviewer checks adequacy; a human decides the required acceptance.

